e can see  trolley problems as an example or a set  of examples of that sort of dynamic and  we should think about our fascination  with these problems the fact that we're  constantly generating more and more  variants of these and piling new memes  on top of other memes and that these  proliferate what is our fascination with  tying people to train tracks and then  coming up with all sorts of ideas about  what's going to happen to them and who's  going to decide on what basis what's  going to happen so these are you know  some interesting thought-provoking  questions to consider these are just 10  out of the vast variety of trolley  problems that I've seen myself and I  know there's got to be hundreds more out  there that I haven't seen and people are  constantly generating them so if you've  really got a kick out of this I'm game  for creating more 10 trolley problem  memes with a little bit of explanation  or examination of them so you know you  can leave a comment or give it a thumbs  up or whatever it is that you want to do  maybe share it on some of the sites  where people  kick these problems around and yeah I'll  keep at it  you
 

